          "id": "c3a17efc34c393430e3e2e7b222b2ec73d10d8a0",
          "message": "perf: skip duplicate Linux accept rearm\n\nSkip duplicate worker-level accept re-arms on Linux epoll accept events by marking successful accept completions with the existing cqeFMore flag.\n\nAlso add clean CPU/resource benchmark evidence, Linux accept re-arm evidence, bench module replace-path normalization, and documentation for KRUDA_READ_BUF_SIZE=2048 as an optional short-header memory profile candidate. This keeps Kruda defaults unchanged and intentionally excludes the rejected io_uring, CPU affinity, PGO, and speculative-read experiments.",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-06T18:16:57+07:00",
