          "distinct": true,
          "id": "88acc18245d2a275aa3758cd99b7a91ee2a4e72c",
          "message": "fix(wing): XFF dedicated fields and segmentation-independent 431\n\n* fix(wing): parse X-Forwarded-For/X-Real-IP into dedicated fields; 431 for oversized header line\n\nTwo adopter-visible correctness fixes deferred from the body-limit review:\n\n- TrustProxy: X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP were stored in the 8-slot generic\n  extra-header array, so a request with >8 unknown headers dropped them and\n  RemoteAddr fell back to the socket peer. Parse them into dedicated request\n  fields via knownHeader's length-dispatch (len 15 / 9) — zero cost on the\n  no-XFF hot path since hot-path header lengths never reach those cases.\n- classifyIncomplete now flags a single header line over HeaderLimit as\n  parseHeaderTooLarge so tryParse returns 431 instead of a silent close.\n  Slow-path only; the hot path never calls the classifier.\n\n* fix(wing): make 431 verdict segmentation-independent + takeover parity\n\nAddresses review of the 431 change:\n- classifyIncomplete no longer rejects on accumulated total bytes before the\n  header block is complete. That made the verdict depend on TCP segmentation: a\n  small-line/large-total header block was served when it arrived in one read but\n  431'd when split. Oversized headers are now caught per-line once the block is\n  complete, with the read buffer as the total backstop.\n- takeoverLoop now answers 431 for an oversized header line on a pipelined\n  request instead of grouping it with malformed and closing silently.\n- X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP: first header wins (net/http Get semantics) when a\n  request carries duplicates.\n\n* fix(wing): empty-first XFF wins, takeover buffer honors ReadBufSize, case-insensitive XFF lookup\n\nJoint-review findings:\n- X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP first-header-wins used the stored value as the\n  'seen' sentinel, so an empty first header let a later (attacker-supplied) value\n  override it. Track 'seen' explicitly so the first header wins even when empty\n  (net/http Get semantics) and RemoteAddr falls back to the socket peer.\n- takeoverLoop used a fixed 8 KB pool buffer; with HeaderLimit > 8 KB it\n  truncated leftover and wrongly 431'd legal large headers that the event loop\n  accepts. Grow the buffer to ReadBufSize (returned to the pool by the defer).\n- Header()/RawHeader() now match X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP case-insensitively,\n  restoring the lookup behavior they had as generic extra headers.\n\n* fix(wing): prevent oversized buffer retention in takeoverBufPool\n\nWhen the takeover path grows the pool buffer beyond the default 8 KB\n(to match ReadBufSize for large HeaderLimit configs), the deferred\ncleanup now returns the original pool-sized buffer to the pool and\nlets the grown buffer be reclaimed by the GC. Previously the grown\nbuffer was returned to the pool, causing permanent oversized-buffer\nretention.\n\nAlso add TestWing_HeaderLineLengthBoundary which pins the exact\noff-by-one contract of classifyIncomplete: len(hline) == HeaderLimit\nis accepted, len(hline) == HeaderLimit+1 yields 431.",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-16T00:23:29+07:00",
