          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f1243093c2707b16171885cea389ce105d28336f",
          "message": "fix(wing): close takeover File on shutdown to prevent fd double-close\n\n- Mark the conn takenOver at Takeover dispatch.\n- The doneCh drain and a new post-drain sweep close each Takeover *os.File so\n  the fd is released during shutdown instead of leaking to a finalizer that\n  could later close a recycled fd.\n- The cleanup loop skips closeFd for takenOver conns, so a Takeover fd is\n  closed exactly once across both the event-loop and Takeover shutdown paths.\n\nVerified on Linux/epoll: the new test is a deterministic red before the fix\n(accept4: bad file descriptor) and green after; hot-path bench A/B is parity.",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-19T22:55:23+07:00",
          "tree_id": "93d4ac67743586fffcfb8dd946fe3d54b8cb30f8",
          "url": "https://github.com/go-kruda/kruda/commit/f1243093c2707b16171885cea389ce105d28336f"
