          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e17356a890ae7a60a91772e68e4f1d2e0a3460d5",
          "message": "feat(wing): SSE and incremental streaming on the Wing transport\n\nMakes c.SSE() and c.Stream() work on Wing (default on Linux) via the kruda.Stream route preset — previously they errored unless the route ran on net/http. A dedicated wingStreamWriter streams chunks to the takeover *os.File (hot path untouched); client disconnect cancels the handler context; a stuck client is bounded by WriteTimeout; fasthttp gets an actionable error; TestClient.SSE() helper added. Reviewed per-task + whole-branch (opus) + codex (caught and fixed a header-flush bug); Linux/epoll -race validated on tiger; alloc guards stay 0.",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-28T12:41:54+07:00",
          "tree_id": "ae5e07e1c1bc9091a2748aa0750c9504bf853e58",
